course: dictionary
lesson: 4731
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Read the words around it first. «The cyclist sounded her horn at the corner.» Cyclists do not grow horns, so horn here must mean the device that makes a loud warning noise.
explain: «The goat lowered its horns and charged.» The clues are goat and charged. A horn is a hard, pointed growth on an animal's head. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then put your meaning in place of the word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «The French horn played a soft, low tune in the orchestra.» Orchestra and tune point to a brass instrument you blow into. The spelling is the same every time, so the context does the work.
fact: Horn can mean a hard, pointed growth on the head of an animal, like a cow, goat, rhino or ram.
fact: A horn is also the device in a car, bus or bike that makes a loud warning sound. You beep or sound the horn.
fact: The French horn is a brass musical instrument in the orchestra. You blow into it.
fact: Horns are made of keratin, the same stuff as hair and fingernails. Horns are hard, but they are not bone.
fact: The phrase «lock horns» means to argue, and «take the bull by the horns» means to face a problem bravely.
exercise: «The rhino lowered its horn before the charge.» What is a rhino's horn? | *A hard, pointed growth on its head | A loud warning sound | A brass instrument | A kind of tail
exercise: «Dad tapped the horn to warn the cyclist.» What does horn mean here? | A brass instrument in an orchestra | A place where cows are kept | A hard growth on an animal's head | *A device that makes a loud warning sound
exercise: «Rhino horns are made of keratin, the same stuff as hair and nails.» What is keratin? | A kind of cloud | A loud warning sound | *The hard material that horns, hair and nails are made of | A brass metal used in instruments
test: «The two rivals locked horns about who would lead the team.» What does locked horns mean? | Sounded a warning | Built a fence | *Argued | Hugged tightly
test: «When wolves come, musk oxen form a ring with their horns facing out.» What are the horns in this sentence? | Loud car warnings | Long blades of grass | *Hard, pointed growths on the head | Brass instruments
exam: «Vikings did not wear horned helmets in battle; the horns come from costumes made for an opera in 1876.» Which is true? | Horns are a brass instrument | *The horns came from opera costumes, not from real Viking battles | Keratin is a kind of costume | Vikings wore horned helmets in every battle
